gaxt(){return"The calendar shows all meetings and payments. Tap an event to open the right app. Be more than an hour late to a meeting and the deal falls through."},
gaxH(){return"DetalBuy sells parts. OEM is reliable; aftermarket and used are cheaper but may fail again. A part only fits its own make and model."},
gaxL(){return"Plates: a nice number adds value to a car. Roll one at the traffic police or buy from the showcase \u2014 then put it on a car before selling."},
gaxw(){return"Construction is a side job. Place slabs straight: overhang gets cut off. You\u2019re paid per slab, up to 8 game hours a day."},
gaxJ(){return"PlameBlocks is a puzzle to kill waiting time. While you play, game time runs faster."},
gaxE(){return"Drive Ace is a highway race. While driving, time runs three times faster, and you\u2019re paid per kilometer."},
gaxT(){return"Taxi Park: drive yourself or hire drivers. Give them your car and they hand in the takings once a day."},
gaxu(){return"Car Wash is a side job. Wash customers\u2019 cars clean and fast: great work earns tips, and your rate grows with experience."},
gaxQ(){return"Scrapyard: wrecked cars below their value. Buy, restore via DetalBuy and a garage, sell for more. You can also strip your own car for parts."},
gaxz(){return"Dealership is your own business. Put cars on display, hire sellers \u2014 it sells on its own. But rent and salaries are due every week."},
gaxp(){return"Auction: lots you won\u2019t find in the feed. Inspect before bidding and don\u2019t go over your limit \u2014 rivals bluff too."},
gaxx(){return"Containers are blind auctions. Clues help, but one may lie. Inside there can be treasure or junk."},
gaxB(){return"Flights: cars from Europe. You need a foreign passport and a visa from GosBuy. On site you\u2019ll see what the seller didn\u2019t mention."},
gaxF(){return"Import: cars to order from Japan, Korea, China and the UAE. Check the auction sheet grade: \u201cR\u201d means damaged."},
